{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"string-methods","title":"String Methods","group":"Types, Values & Operators","order":10,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Every string method returns a new string (or a value) — the original never changes.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Cheat sheet</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Example → result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>includes / startsWith / endsWith</code></td><td>Search → boolean</td><td><code>'hello'.startsWith('he')</code> → <code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>indexOf / lastIndexOf</code></td><td>Position or <code>-1</code></td><td><code>'banana'.indexOf('a')</code> → <code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>slice(start, end)</code></td><td>Substring; negatives count from end</td><td><code>'hello'.slice(-3)</code> → <code>'llo'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>toUpperCase / toLowerCase</code></td><td>Case</td><td><code>'Hi'.toUpperCase()</code> → <code>'HI'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>trim / trimStart / trimEnd</code></td><td>Remove whitespace</td><td><code>' x '.trim()</code> → <code>'x'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>padStart / padEnd</code></td><td>Pad to a length</td><td><code>'5'.padStart(3, '0')</code> → <code>'005'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>repeat(n)</code></td><td>Repeat</td><td><code>'ab'.repeat(3)</code> → <code>'ababab'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>split(sep)</code></td><td>String → array</td><td><code>'a,b'.split(',')</code> → <code>['a', 'b']</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>replace / replaceAll</code></td><td>Substitute (string or regex)</td><td><code>'a-a'.replaceAll('-', '+')</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>at(i)</code></td><td>Index with negatives</td><td><code>'abc'.at(-1)</code> → <code>'c'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>localeCompare</code></td><td>Locale-aware compare for sorting</td><td><code>'a'.localeCompare('b')</code> → <code>-1</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>In action</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const text = \"  The quick brown fox  \";\nconst t = text.trim();\nconsole.log(`[${t}]`, t.length);\nconsole.log(t.includes(\"quick\"), t.indexOf(\"o\"), t.lastIndexOf(\"o\"));\nconsole.log(t.split(\" \"), t.split(\" \", 2));\nconsole.log(t.replace(\"o\", \"0\"), \"|\", t.replaceAll(\"o\", \"0\"));\nconsole.log(t.replace(/o/g, (m) =&gt; m.toUpperCase()));\nconsole.log(\"7\".padStart(3, \"0\"), \"ab\".padEnd(5, \".\"), \"=\".repeat(5));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[The quick brown fox] 19\ntrue 12 17\n[ 'The', 'quick', 'brown', 'fox' ] [ 'The', 'quick' ]\nThe quick br0wn fox | The quick br0wn f0x\nThe quick brOwn fOx\n007 ab... =====</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>replace</code> with a <strong>string</strong> pattern replaces only the <em>first</em> match. Use <code>replaceAll</code>, or a regex with the <code>g</code> flag.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-puzzle\"></i>Common interview manipulations</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const reverse = (s) =&gt; [...s].reverse().join(\"\");\nconst isPalindrome = (s) =&gt; {\n  const clean = s.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, \"\");\n  return clean === reverse(clean);\n};\nconst capitalize = (s) =&gt; s.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.slice(1);\nconst titleCase = (s) =&gt; s.split(\" \").map(capitalize).join(\" \");\nconst countChars = (s) =&gt;\n  [...s].reduce((acc, ch) =&gt; ({ ...acc, [ch]: (acc[ch] ?? 0) + 1 }), {});\n\nconsole.log(reverse(\"hello\"));\nconsole.log(isPalindrome(\"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\"));\nconsole.log(titleCase(\"learn via notes\"));\nconsole.log(countChars(\"banana\"));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>olleh\ntrue\nLearn Via Notes\n{ b: 1, a: 3, n: 2 }</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-cut\"></i>substring vs slice vs substr</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Negative indices</th><th>start &gt; end</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>slice(s, e)</code></td><td>Count from end</td><td>Returns <code>''</code></td><td>Use this</td></tr><tr><td><code>substring(s, e)</code></td><td>Treated as <code>0</code></td><td>Swaps the arguments</td><td>OK</td></tr><tr><td><code>substr(s, len)</code></td><td>Start may be negative</td><td>Second arg is a <em>length</em></td><td>Deprecated</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do you reverse a string in JavaScript?</summary><div><p><code>[...s].reverse().join('')</code>. Strings have no <code>reverse</code>, so convert to an array first; spread (rather than <code>split('')</code>) keeps emoji and other surrogate pairs intact.</p></div></details></section>"}